---
title: Roast leg of lamb with gravy
servings: 6
yield: 6 to 8 servings
tags: [lamb, easter, passover, holiday, spring]
time: 3 hours 15 minutes
source: Roast Lamb Leg with Gravy by Nagi Maehashi, RecipeTin Eats, https://www.recipetineats.com/roast-lamb-leg-with-gravy/
---

Take the @lamb leg{2.75-3%kg}(bone-in) out of the fridge at least ~{1%hour} before roasting.

Heat the oven to 240°C (475°F), or 220°C fan, with a shelf in the middle.

Mix the @rosemary{1.5%tbsp}(leaves, finely chopped), @garlic{3%cloves}(finely minced) and @olive oil{2%tbsp}.

Set the @garlic{2%heads}(halved crosswise) cut side up in a #roasting pan{} with a few sprigs of @rosemary{}(optional). Sit the lamb on top. Rub it all over with the rosemary mixture, then sprinkle with the @fine salt{1.5%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Roast ~{20%minutes}.

Turn the oven down to 200°C (400°F), or 180°C fan. Roast ~{1%hour} more, until the thickest part reads 53°C (127°F). Start checking at 45 minutes.

Move the lamb to a plate, cover loosely with foil and rest ~{20-60%minutes}. It finishes at about 62°C (144°F), medium-rare.

== Gravy ==

Throw out the rosemary sprigs. Leave about 4 to 5 tbsp of fat in the pan: pour some off if there is more, add @unsalted butter{} if there is less.

Set the pan over medium heat. When the fat bubbles, stir in the @all-purpose flour{4%tbsp} and cook ~{1%minute}.

Stir in half the @beef broth{2.5%cup}(low-sodium) until smooth, then the rest. Mash the roasted garlic into it with a #potato masher{}.

Simmer a couple of minutes, stirring, until it starts to thicken. Take it off the heat a little thin, because it keeps thickening. Taste for seasoning.

Strain into a jug, pressing on the garlic.

> Trust the thermometer, not the clock. Legs vary a lot in thickness.
